  "cues": [
    {
      "start_seconds": 0.0,
      "end_seconds": 2.7093333333333334,
      "text": "A processor asks memory for a number."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 2.7093333333333334,
      "end_seconds": 5.738666666666667,
      "text": "Why can it not just take the answer immediately?"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 5.738666666666667,
      "end_seconds": 12.303958333333334,
      "text": "Let us slow one read down, and follow two numbers that look similar but mean very different things."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 12.399999999999991,
      "end_seconds": 14.426666666666659,
      "text": "The first number is sixteen."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 14.426666666666659,
      "end_seconds": 18.053333333333324,
      "text": "Think of it as a location, like a numbered slot."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 18.053333333333324,
      "end_seconds": 22.149333333333324,
      "text": "The second number is forty two: the value stored in that slot."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 22.149333333333324,
      "end_seconds": 23.98399999999999,
      "text": "An address answers where."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 23.98399999999999,
      "end_seconds": 26.181333333333324,
      "text": "The stored value answers what."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 26.300000000000182,
      "end_seconds": 29.457333333333516,
      "text": "The processor puts sixteen on the address lines."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 29.457333333333516,
      "end_seconds": 32.59333333333352,
      "text": "Follow that selection into the memory table."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 32.59333333333352,
      "end_seconds": 36.19600000000018,
      "text": "It picks one row, and that row contains forty two."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 36.19600000000018,
      "end_seconds": 42.21062500000018,
      "text": "Changing the address would select a different row, not change the number inside this row."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 42.30000000000014,
      "end_seconds": 46.7872916666668,
      "text": "But selecting a row and receiving its contents are separate events."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 46.7872916666668,
      "end_seconds": 53.97395833333347,
      "text": "In our teaching model, the data lines still show an old value, nineteen, while memory prepares the answer."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 53.97395833333347,
      "end_seconds": 55.89395833333347,
      "text": "Those lines carry a number."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 55.89395833333347,
      "end_seconds": 58.90195833333347,
      "text": "That alone does not make it the right number."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 58.99999999999994,
      "end_seconds": 60.855999999999945,
      "text": "Imagine sampling now."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 60.855999999999945,
      "end_seconds": 67.93729166666661,
      "text": "The processor would capture nineteen, even though we asked for location sixteen and expected forty two."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 67.93729166666661,
      "end_seconds": 70.3052916666666,
      "text": "The mistake is not arithmetic."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 70.3052916666666,
      "end_seconds": 74.91191666666661,
      "text": "We have confused a value that is present with a value that is ready."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 74.99999999999972,
      "end_seconds": 80.01333333333305,
      "text": "Now memory presents forty two and indicates that the data is valid."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 80.01333333333305,
      "end_seconds": 85.47466666666638,
      "text": "Under this model's rules, the processor samples only after that indication."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 85.47466666666638,
      "end_seconds": 87.77866666666638,
      "text": "The address stays sixteen throughout."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 87.77866666666638,
      "end_seconds": 91.75395833333305,
      "text": "What changes is our permission to trust the returned data."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 91.86666666666596,
      "end_seconds": 95.36533333333263,
      "text": "We can draw the same story as a timing diagram."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 95.36533333333263,
      "end_seconds": 97.5199999999993,
      "text": "A read request comes first."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 97.5199999999993,
      "end_seconds": 99.58933333333263,
      "text": "Data becomes valid later."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 99.58933333333263,
      "end_seconds": 102.76799999999929,
      "text": "Sampling occurs inside that valid interval."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 102.76799999999929,
      "end_seconds": 110.73729166666597,
      "text": "The traces share one time axis; they are three views of the same transaction, not three unrelated pictures."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 110.83333333333205,
      "end_seconds": 113.11599999999872,
      "text": "So keep these questions separate."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 113.11599999999872,
      "end_seconds": 114.80133333333205,
      "text": "Where should memory look?"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 114.80133333333205,
      "end_seconds": 116.33733333333205,
      "text": "That is the address."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 116.33733333333205,
      "end_seconds": 119.06799999999872,
      "text": "When can the processor use the answer?"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 119.06799999999872,
      "end_seconds": 121.09466666666538,
      "text": "That is the validity rule."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 121.09466666666538,
      "end_seconds": 126.52799999999871,
      "text": "The important idea is an agreement about when information becomes trustworthy."
    }
  ],
